    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is primed for a high-ceiling performance tonight, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier efficiency score of 81.88. His matchup against Holmes is ideal, benefiting from a robust 18% boost due to the pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a strong 14% platoon advantage. **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) also grades out as an elite play, drawing a favorable 4.59 xERA matchup and maximizing his value by hitting in the leadoff spot. We are also leaning into the speed element today; **Jackson Merrill** (68.51) and **Nasim Nunez** (62.15) are high-priority starts, both capitalizing on matchups against pitchers with slow deliveries, which significantly elevates their stolen base probability in a category where every tick counts.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board was keeping **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** on the bench with a 54.41 score. While his matchup against Rodriguez offers a decent SP skill boost, his projected platoon disadvantage (-15%) and a lower-order lineup placement ultimately pushed him behind the utility efficiency of **Curtis Mead**. We are also closely monitoring **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**; both are facing the tough arm of Manaea, but their scores are buoyed by elite historical BvP data, effectively shielding them from a deeper slide in our rankings. While **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the bench with a 51.46 score\u2014a result of a harsh platoon hit\u2014he remains our premier \"break-glass\" option should any late-scratch news emerge. We have no major weather concerns to report, but owners should keep an eye on lineup configurations for **Jacob Wilson** and **Sam Antonacci** to ensure their leadoff roles remain solidified.",
